+`/v1/ns/erase`
+--------------
+
+This endpoint erases an account, with the same semantics as `NS ERASE`: it deletes all records of the account, unregisters the channels it founded, and disconnects every client logged in to it. The name can then be registered again. The request is a JSON object with fields:
+
+* `accountName`: string, name of the account
+
+The response is a JSON object with fields:
+
+* `success`: whether the account was erased
+* `errorCode`: string, optional, machine-readable description of the error. Possible values include: `INVALID_REQUEST`, `ACCOUNT_DOES_NOT_EXIST`, `UNKNOWN_ERROR`.
+* `error`: string, optional, human-readable description of the failure if `errorCode` is `UNKNOWN_ERROR`
+
